$ Tiny non-square minesweeper for testing.  Standard convention: minesweeper.eprime
$ declares `find grid : matrix indexed by [int(1..height), int(1..width)]`, so
$ index[0] is the row axis (= height) and index[1] is the column axis (= width).
$ Used as a control case alongside the kakuro non-square test — both should
$ produce puzzle.width=3, puzzle.height=2.
language ESSENCE' 1.0

letting width be 3
letting height be 2

letting known be [
[true,  true,  true],
[true,  true,  true]
]

letting mines be [
[false, true,  false],
[false, false, false]
]
